dif: def"
A reversible difference between two identified states.

The goal is to let QPS carry an active implementation change as a
reversible object: apply a candidate state, test it, and return to the
previous proven state if the candidate fails.

Structural identity should be preferred over line-only targeting.
Paths and line coordinates remain useful source coordinates.

The exact representation and execution semantics remain to be discovered
through implementation.
";

