checkpoint: (
pipeline- "prepare -> inspect exact lowered document -> emit only when supported -> validate exact candidate -> publish exact candidate";
semantic_lowering- "Source-neutral semantic lowering is promoted into the shared candidate-generation path";
support_before_emit- "Unsupported semantics stop before emission and own no candidate bytes";
candidate_identity- "Publication commits the exact candidate bytes validated by the proven ConversionPlan";
boolean_truth- "qps cipher test returns true only when exact candidate generation, semantic support, QPS validation, and no-write truth all succeed";
runtime_sequence- "RuntimeValue SEQUENCE exists as a distinct runtime value and supports nested heterogeneous values";
key_namespace- "Key is a file-inside-file namespace whose paragraph boundary is the first blank line at the Key's own structural depth";
navigation_syntax- "Authored declarations use key. term: item-, while structural navigation uses dot traversal and final - only as an explicit Item/value expectation";
reference_syntax- "[>key.term.item-] is the canonical explicit Item reference; the - is inside the reference and requires the final target to resolve as an Item";
source_spans- "Key, Term, and Item own truthful source start/end lines; scope and probe render the exact physical span owned by the selected structural address";
structural_resolution- "Structural navigation resolves hierarchical identity independently from source ownership; nested source remains part of its containing structural span";
item_assertion- "Authored Semantic_Walk reserves the final segment for structure_item when selects_item_value is true and rejects an existing Term when Item identity was explicitly required";
execution_dispatch- "Execution definitions delegate ordinary control-flow statements to the common statement grammar; -while now parses and executes inside named execution definitions";
semantic_walk- "Semantic_Walk parses as a named ExecutionDefinition, executes successfully, and matches native structural selection including TERM_IS_NOT_ITEM rejection";
root_authority- "_index.qps is the current QPS navigation authority; obsolete qps/qps/docs/QPS.qps and its stale golden test were removed";
navigation_stack- "structural selection, grammar regression, semantic walk, probe CLI, and scope CLI are green together";
language_diversion- "The structural-language diversion now also proves canonical [>item-] reference boundaries, Term-owned executable bodies as term: {...};, and full-expression Item values without requiring % calculation syntax";
item_expression- "Ordinary Items may bind full QPS expressions through the shared expression grammar; arithmetic no longer requires % when the intended result is an Item";
term_execution_body- "A Term may own an executable body as term: {...}; the Term carries semantic identity and the braces carry executable contents";
calculation_compatibility- "%target: expression remains supported compatibility syntax while Item-bound expressions are the simpler canonical form when the result is a value";
root_qps_reference- "Root _index.qps now records the concise QPS utilization rules for primitive identity, complete [>item-] references, Item expressions, Term execution bodies, and % compatibility";
checklist_workflow- "qps checklist is now authored in qps/qps/checklist.qps above generic native module, document, sequence, structural-introspection, and write primitives; each invocation regenerates ephemeral Checklist numbering, renders DONE Checklists, exposes visible tasks, and resolves exact Checklist/task addresses";
execution_registry- "ExecutionEngine registration now stores neutral execution identity, body, domain, and source facts rather than retaining ExecutionDefinitionNode as the runtime registry identity; the build and unaffected execution stack are green";
);

