task_9: (
identity- "checklist.nominal_agent_workflow";
summary- "Establish the CE-OS repository-memory workflow across _index.qps, checklist.qps, Save, and History so agents can work without conversational memory";
state- "active";

product- "CE-OS has a systematic repository-memory model where _index.qps owns durable current truth and usage, checklist.qps owns unfinished work and implementation memory, and history.qps owns accepted completed transitions; an agent can enter a subsystem, understand it, resume work, preserve discoveries in the correct authority, and explicitly Save completed tasks without human babysitting";

memory_model: (
index- "_index.qps describes what the containing repository area currently is, how its QPS surfaces are used, its durable capabilities, interfaces, rules, and operational truth";
checklist- "checklist.qps describes unfinished work: goals, implementation steps, blockers, discoveries, decisions, proof in progress, and deferred work";
history- "history.qps records accepted completed transitions and their provenance; it is not the authority for how the current system is used";
);

placement_rules: (
durable_truth- "If completing work establishes information needed to understand or use the resulting subsystem, update the closest appropriate _index.qps before the task becomes complete";
current_work- "If a discovery is required to finish the current objective, add it to the current task as working memory";
deferred_work- "If a discovery should be implemented later, create a task in the checklist.qps belonging to the repository area that owns the future implementation";
accepted_work- "After explicit Save accepts a complete task, History preserves the accepted transition and the task is deleted from current_work.tasks";
);

documentation_rule: (
decision- "Every nontrivial task must explicitly decide whether completion changes durable subsystem knowledge";
required- "When durable knowledge changes, the task identifies the _index.qps authority that must be updated and proves that update before completion";
not_required- "When implementation preserves already-documented behavior, the task may explicitly record that no _index.qps change is required and why";
save_boundary- "Save does not invent or repair subsystem documentation; documentation obligations must already be satisfied before the task reaches complete";
);

documentation: (
required- true;
authority- "_index.qps";
goal- "Keep the root CE-OS usage and repository-memory authority synchronized with the Checklist, Save, and History workflow established by this task";
state- "active";
proof- "Root _index.qps already documents the repository-memory model and current Checklist/Save contract; any later workflow changes made by this task must update that authority before completion";
);

current: (
item_1- "qps checklist discovers connected checklist.qps files and regenerates ephemeral Checklist numbering";
item_2- "repository-root checklist.qps is the canonical Checklist workflow/example and naturally appears as Checklist 1";
item_3- "qps checklist <checklist-index> <task-number> resolves the exact authored task structurally";
item_4- "exact task inspection renders the complete authored source span, making the task a schema-independent persistent memory object";
item_5- "complete tasks remain visible while awaiting explicit Save";
item_6- "named reusable execution migration is complete but remains visible because it has not yet been moved through the new Save lifecycle";
item_7- "the concise Checklist index now displays authored task state for every visible task";
item_8- "root _index.qps now permanently defines the repository-memory placement methodology and current Checklist/Save contract";
item_9- "The authored Save transaction is proven end-to-end on disposable History and Checklist authorities; the public qps save N T command has not yet been cut over to it";
);

steps: (

step_1: (
goal- "Provide a concise repository-wide qps checklist index with ephemeral Checklist/task addresses";
product- "A user or agent can discover current work without knowing repository paths";
state- "complete";
);

step_2: (
goal- "Make qps checklist <checklist-index> <task-number> render the complete authored task source span";
product- "A selected task is persistent implementation memory and can evolve without changing Checklist rendering code";
state- "complete";
);

step_3: (
goal- "Create repository-root checklist.qps as the canonical Checklist workflow and example";
product- "An unfamiliar agent has an authored starting point for learning the work-management interface";
state- "complete";
);

step_4: (
goal- "Show authored task state explicitly in concise qps checklist output";
product- "The repository work index visibly distinguishes ready, active, waiting, blocked, and complete work";
state- "complete";
);

step_5: (
goal- "Promote the repository-memory methodology into the appropriate _index.qps authority surfaces";
product- "Agents have durable instructions for deciding whether knowledge belongs in _index.qps, checklist.qps, or history.qps rather than depending on this task or chat";
state- "complete";
);

step_6: (
goal- "Make documentation disposition an explicit completion concern for nontrivial tasks";
product- "A task cannot quietly establish new user-facing or architectural truth while leaving the applicable _index.qps stale";
state- "complete";
);

step_7: (
goal- "Prove complete work remains visible and identifiable until explicit Save";
product- "Finished but unaccepted work cannot silently disappear or be confused with accepted History";
state- "complete";
);

step_8: (
goal- "Define and prove qps save <checklist-index> <task-number> against a disposable authored Checklist task";
product- "Save explicitly selects one complete task, validates it, and either accepts the whole transition or changes nothing";
state- "complete";
);

step_9: (
goal- "Make the completed task itself the authoritative semantic input to Save";
product- "Agents do not maintain a duplicate history_candidate representation of the same accomplishment";
state- "complete";
);

step_10: (
goal- "Prove successful Save publishes normalized History and deletes the accepted task from current_work.tasks";
product- "Checklist contains current/future work while History permanently owns accepted completed work";
state- "active";
);

step_11: (
goal- "Prove failed, malformed, incomplete, interrupted, and duplicate Save attempts preserve Checklist and History integrity";
product- "Agents can use Save without a human guarding transaction correctness";
state- "waiting";
);

step_12: (
goal- "Finish permanent agent-facing documentation and prove the complete workflow from a fresh repository entry point";
product- "Codex can enter CE-OS, read _index.qps, discover work, inspect task memory, maintain discoveries, document durable truth, complete work, Save it, and recover History without prior conversation";
state- "waiting";
);

);

future_application: (
item_1- "After this infrastructure is nominal, an agent can inventory a repository area such as UI/ and improve its _index.qps current-truth documentation while creating appropriately located checklist.qps tasks for unfinished or future work";
item_2- "Repository-wide task creation is future content work performed using this methodology, not part of implementing the Checklist mechanism itself";
);

findings: (
finding_1- "Checklist is most useful as a living authored work document rather than a rigid CLI-owned task schema";
finding_2- "_index.qps and checklist.qps are complementary: the index explains the current system while the Checklist explains work that has not yet become current truth";
finding_3- "Permanent knowledge should not remain trapped in completed Checklist tasks because accepted tasks are deleted after Save";
finding_4- "History records that a transition was accepted, but the applicable _index.qps remains the authority for how the resulting system currently works";
finding_5- "Exact task rendering must remain schema-blind so agents can add useful working-memory structures without extending the CLI";
finding_6- "Generic file_read is now proven byte-exact through authored QPS execution; ordinary qps execution also emits QPS_LOG diagnostics on stdout, so authored-output witnesses must isolate payload from runtime diagnostics";
finding_7- "Generic publish_files now proves arbitrary two-file publication from authored QPS without Checklist, History, task-state, or Save-specific native policy";
finding_8- "Nested Dictionary values were already supported by QPS; Dictionary-valued Items require the Dictionary terminator plus the owning Item terminator, producing the canonical ]; ; boundary as ];;";
finding_9- "QPS structural source ownership is line-based rather than byte-offset based, so generic file_without_span uses the same authored line coordinate model as structure_start, structure_end, and file_span";
finding_10- "Generic file_without_span is proven exact and gives authored QPS a schema-independent way to construct a source document with one structurally selected line span removed";
finding_11- "CE-OS History is one repository-root parseable semantic ledger; repository locality belongs to each accepted entry through authored scope, and qps history <path> is the normal access surface regardless of ledger size";
finding_12- "The disposable authored Save transaction proved that a completed task can directly supply identity, summary, meaning, scope, proof, relevant paths, remaining work, and documentation state without a duplicate history_candidate object";
);

decisions: (
decision_1- "Repository-root checklist.qps remains the permanent Checklist workflow/example and first discovered Checklist";
decision_2- "qps checklist is concise navigation while qps checklist N T exposes the entire selected task";
decision_3- "Current-task discoveries stay with the current task when required for completion; deferred discoveries become tasks where their implementation belongs";
decision_4- "A complete task remains visible until an explicit Save command accepts it";
decision_5- "Successful Save deletes the accepted task rather than retaining a saved task in current_work.tasks";
decision_6- "The completed task is the semantic source for History normalization; Save should not require duplicate manually maintained history content";
decision_7- "Save does not substitute for _index.qps maintenance";
decision_8- "Checklist behavior remains authored in QPS above generic native substrate";
decision_9- "CE-OS owns exactly one history.qps ledger at repository root; subdirectories never receive local History ledgers";
decision_10- "History locality is semantic: Save records repository scope and acceptance timestamp, and qps history <path> queries the root ledger for entries associated with that repository structure";
);

proof: (
proof_1- "qps checklist discovers the root, native-runtime, and authored-language Checklists with fresh numbering";
proof_2- "qps checklist 3 9 resolves task_9 and renders its complete physical source span";
proof_3- "repository-root checklist.qps parses and naturally appears as Checklist 1";
proof_4- "complete native.named_policy_migration remains visible pending explicit Save";
proof_5- "the exact-task renderer accepts arbitrary additional authored task structure without schema-specific changes";
proof_6- "qps checklist now renders complete, waiting, ready, and active states directly in the concise global index";
proof_7- "root _index.qps parses with the permanent repository-memory model and no longer contains the stale hidden-complete or history_candidate Save rules";
proof_8- "repository-root checklist.qps provides the canonical documentation disposition example, and task_9 carries its own explicit required _index.qps documentation obligation";
proof_9- "native.named_policy_migration is authored state complete, remains visible in the global Checklist index, and remains fully inspectable through qps checklist 2 1 without any Save mutation";
proof_10- "generic file_read returns exact file bytes to authored QPS; the earlier mismatch was runtime log output surrounding the authored payload rather than file_read corruption";
proof_11- "generic publish_files successfully replaces two independent files from one authored QPS call and leaves no staged or backup artifacts after successful publication";
proof_12- "generic file_without_span returns the exact remaining file bytes after removing an inclusive authored line span and contains no Checklist or History policy";
proof_13- "A disposable authored Save transaction accepted one complete task, generated a UTC timestamped scoped History entry, removed exactly that task, preserved unrelated work, reparsed both candidate documents, and published them successfully";
proof_14- "The disposable Save proof used the completed task itself as the semantic source and contained no history_candidate surface";
);

next- "Cut the public qps save <checklist-index> <task-number> command over to authored Save task resolution and prove the CLI lifecycle on disposable repository state before accepting real task 2.task_1";

done_when: (
condition_1- "A fresh agent can learn the repository-memory methodology from permanent repository authority without chat context";
condition_2- "qps checklist exposes every current or complete-unsaved task with explicit state";
condition_3- "qps checklist N T exposes enough complete task memory to resume nontrivial work";
condition_4- "Tasks explicitly resolve any required _index.qps documentation before becoming complete";
condition_5- "Required current discoveries remain in the active task and deferred discoveries become tasks in their owning implementation area";
condition_6- "Complete work remains visible until explicit Save";
condition_7- "qps save N T accepts only a valid complete task and makes no mutation on validation failure";
condition_8- "Successful Save publishes normalized semantic History and deletes the accepted source task";
condition_9- "Failed and duplicate Save cases preserve Checklist and History integrity";
condition_10- "Saved accomplishments remain recoverable through qps history while current usage truth remains in the applicable _index.qps";
);
);
);

);

goal- "Find the irreducible QPS and CE-OS kernel by continuing to move semantic authority inward into authored QPS";

repository- "~/ce-os";

workspace- "One repository and one active workspace";

current_state- "The reference-planner and Engineering experiment worktrees have been promoted into ~/ce-os and removed";

checklist_state- "Checklist is a reusable authored execution definition and a multi-surface QPS document";

execution_state- "Canonical reusable execution is migrating from redundant {Name: ...} identity toward Term-owned execution bodies authored as name: {...};";

evidence_state- "Checklist_Evidence gathers live observations and authored QPS can assemble evidence and execute Checklist without native evidence-splicing logic";

engineering_state- "The independent Engineering safety-factor specimen is preserved in the main repository and proves authored numeric threshold evaluation without requiring a new generic requirement framework";

build_state- "QPS builds with RuntimeValue SEQUENCE, canonical [>item-] references, full-expression Item values, Term-owned execution-body parsing, truthful structural spans, and the existing runtime/math regressions green";

active- "Finish Cipher foreign and structured semantics until real Engineering conversion satisfies exact boolean truth";

next- "Finish canonical reusable Term execution so name: {...}; can be registered and instantiated, then resume Cipher lowering against the real Engineering witness";

latest_probe- "Canonical kinetic_energy: {...}; parses with [>mass-], [>velocity-], full-expression Item arithmetic, and -return; Item unit suffix, grammar regression, and runtime math tests remain green";

git_checkpoint_state- "Active QPS implementation is checkpointed in Git while intentionally unfinished; the current native suite is 29/36 green with seven red witnesses: Engineering safety-factor syntax, symbol-resolver numeric Item extraction, corpus conformance from three legacy reference forms, test-suite reference_document authority lookup, query CLI legacy [>input]- fixture syntax, and the save CLI fixture still exercising the retired file-path contract instead of qps save <checklist-index> <task-number>";

latest_failure- "Current remaining language seam: the neutral ExecutionEngine registry is proven, but canonical TermDeclarationNode containing an ExecutionBlockNode is not yet registered as a reusable execution; historical Reference_Document parent_depth remains a separate red witness on the old authored execution-definition path";

